 |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ |\n\nThen, we add a column for $¬A∨B.$ Remember that $¬A∨B$ is true if either $¬A$ is true or $B$ is true. \n\n| $\\,A\\,$ | $\\,¬A\\,$ | $\\,B\\,$ | $\\,¬A∨B\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ |"} :step/id #uuid "69e86682-067f-514d-b28b-2707c261c9b0"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186559958 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186410108 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "29224407-55cf-551f-b649-9fde0ff90969" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "P∨¬Q" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186410065} {:answer/id #uuid "70bc8ea3-93c8-58ea-848f-ec99ae31061f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "¬(P∧Q)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186410075} {:answer/id #uuid "72bcfa5c-5b94-5b39-8907-f5e55b173ceb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "¬P∨Q" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186410076} {:answer/id #uuid "b3a7f504-4ca7-5894-b89f-b544a051e640" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "P∧¬Q" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186410085} {:answer/id #uuid "bf299fda-072c-544f-b29f-e8fcc1aa3744" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "¬(P∨Q)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186410086}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186410086} :answer-field/id #uuid "3485fc02-497e-5efc-b575-32abe89dc9c3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186410095}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "e5ae3f5a-c838-553b-8c0d-d176aea1d388" :question/math-academy-id "q-176861" :question/problem "$\\pi $ is **not** a rational or negative number.\n\nExpress the compound statement above in symbolic form given the following:\n\n- $P:\\pi \\text{ is a rational number}$\n\n- $Q:\\pi \\text{ is a negative number}$" :question/worked-solution "The given sentence is the negation of the following sentence: \n\n$\\pi $ is a rational or negative number, \n\nwhich can be expressed symbolically as $P∨Q.$\n\nThe negation is represented by the symbol \"$¬$\".  \n\nTherefore, the given sentence is expressed symbolically as $¬(P∨Q).$"} :step/id #uuid "ad8f3813-98ab-572f-81fe-9dfebf1d8148" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186559971}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186559965 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186374366 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1699e9e8-795a-5ba6-a0ee-4950440932f2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$-1$ is not greater than $-\\sqrt{2}.$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186374368} {:answer/id #uuid "22c73b81-84a1-5c4c-97f7-6262b43bda6a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$-1$ is greater than $-\\sqrt{2}.$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186374369} {:answer/id #uuid "9fd81ddb-0ea4-524f-ab98-1388d627c725" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$-\\sqrt{2}$ is not greater than $-1.$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186374370} {:answer/id #uuid "577cf9a8-c082-5003-946d-75e9eb366f80" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$-1$ is  equal to $-\\sqrt{2}.$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186374371} {:answer/id #uuid "afe1efba-82c0-55ef-aecd-5a961863ad14" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$-\\sqrt{2}$ is greater than $-1.$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186374372}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186374368} :answer-field/id #uuid "ea3ba7f3-2de5-5652-942e-f697424cd57a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186374367}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "9c30bbae-c196-5bdb-9a48-5e29a02258c2" :question/math-academy-id "q-176858" :question/problem "Consider the following statement.\n\n$-1$ is greater than $-\\sqrt{2}.$\n\nWhat is the negation of this statement?" :question/worked-solution "Let's denote the given statement as $P.$\n\nThe symbol \"$¬$\" represents negation. So, our task is to negate the given sentence. \n\nTo negate our plain English sentence, we place the words \"It is not true that\" in front of it. This gives the following:\n\nIt is not true that $-1$ is greater than $-\\sqrt{2}.$\n\nIn other words, $-1$ is *not* greater than $-\\sqrt{2}.$ Therefore, $¬P$ means the following:\n\n$-1$ is **not** greater than $-\\sqrt{2}.$\n\nNote that $P$ is **true,** while $¬P$ is **false.**"} :step/id #uuid "b97e62d1-668c-52b0-8c30-69e44c46ee66" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186559958}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186559971 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186559820 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "65e0597d-70c4-58e1-8e7e-e21efcc693cc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "¬C∧¬D" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186559269} {:answer/id #uuid "7d48af0e-1847-5050-88d7-d15aeacb37df" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "¬(¬C∧D)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186559327} {:answer/id #uuid "8b73bda6-1aa7-5aab-9f40-3b0306647e7f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "¬(C∧D)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186559369} {:answer/id #uuid "c8457e32-4ea1-538b-8fec-08974b2f73aa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "C∧D" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186559502} {:answer/id #uuid "da880646-a80a-5029-b390-32aa365c9e96" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "¬C∧D" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186559553}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186559502} :answer-field/id #uuid "d09dc30c-edd9-55fe-a325-e95e5732ee2c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186559749}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "7d9b9daf-a686-5f9d-9e9b-43c577599d8d" :question/math-academy-id "q-176872" :question/problem "Simplify the statement $¬[¬(¬(¬C)∧D)].$" :question/worked-solution "Two negations in a row cancel each other out. So, we can simplify $¬(¬C)$ to $C.$ \n\nAs a result of this, the statement simplifes to \n\n$$\n¬[¬(C∧D)].\n$$\n\nThen, we can simplify $¬[¬(C∧D)]]$ to $C∧D.$\n\nTherefore, the given statement can be simplified to \n\n$$\nC∧D.\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "cee3ee6d-9bbc-5bff-b8aa-bb3df2a8156d" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186559938}}] :activity/title "The \"Not\" Connective" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186559004}]}
